<h1>Storage scopes and progress notes</h1>
<p>The current release gives provider storage a scope and an optional idle expiry, and gives a run a narrow bounded way to post what it's doing.</p>
</header>
<p class="release-receipt"><strong>{{ release.tag }}</strong> · {{ release.date }} · <a href="{{ release.url }}">Release notes ↗</a> · <a href="{{ release.sourceUrl }}">{{ release.shortRevision }}</a>
</p>
<section id="changes"><span class="compat-anchor" id="release-summary-title" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2>Three changes to storage and progress notes</h2>
<div class="guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Change comparison">
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th scope="col">Change</th>
<th scope="col">Practical consequence</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th scope="row">Storage scopes</th>
<td data-label="Practical consequence"><code>private-conversation</code> keeps today’s per-subject default. <code>shared-conversation</code> and <code>agent</code> give a provider stable storage across authorized callers without sharing gateway conversation history; every caller is still authorized individually.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row">Idle retention</th>
<td data-label="Practical consequence">Opt a provider/scope into <code>retention: {mode: idle-ttl, idleTtlMs: &lt;ms&gt;}</code> and the broker sweeps expired resources at startup and every 12 hours, skipping active leases. The default stays <code>{mode: keep}</code>, so nothing already stored gains a clock.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row">Progress notes</th>
<td data-label="Practical consequence">The shell’s <code>progress "text"</code> builtin, a route’s <code>progressNotes: true</code>, and Slack Agent’s <code>liveness.statusText: true</code> let a run post one short status line without that text becoming the answer.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="migration"><span class="compat-anchor" id="release-details-title" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="compat-anchor" id="release-path-title" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2>Every broker storage constraint needs one edit.</h2>
<p>Replace <code>namespace: chat</code> with <code>scope: private-conversation</code> before the 0.25.0 broker starts — the old key is refused, not translated. Existing private-conversation data keeps its authority-bound continuity and is found unchanged. <a href="{{ source }}/crates/dekopon-brokerd/README.md#optional-provider-storage-and-chat-memory">Provider storage contract ↗</a>.</p>
<p>Coming from before 0.22.0? <code>identityMappings</code> is now <code>principals</code>; <code>chatScopes</code> is gone, with conversation narrowing moved into the Cedar policies that grant capabilities; and <code>constraintSets</code>/<code>credentialByAgent</code> are now per-provider <code>capabilities</code> blocks plus <code>agents.&lt;agent&gt;.credentials</code>. Every Cedar statement needs an <code>@id</code>. Run the new offline <code>dekopon-brokerd check</code> and <code>dekopond check</code> against edited files before rolling either daemon. <a href="/guides/access/#identity">Current identity example</a> · <a href="{{ source }}/docs/upgrading.md">Full upgrade steps ↗</a>
</p>
<p>Six releases landed between here and v0.18.0. The headline items: per-message steering that interrupts only the running model call (v0.24.0), and an OpenRouter model kind beside the existing OpenAI-compatible and ChatGPT clients (v0.20.0). <a href="{{ source }}/CHANGELOG.md">Full changelog ↗</a>
</p>
</section>
<section id="limits"><span class="compat-anchor" id="release-scope-title" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2>Retention deletes; it doesn’t back anything up.</h2>
<p>An idle-TTL sweep only removes storage nobody has touched inside the window you set — there is no export, no encryption at rest, and JSONL dedup stays permanent until its own record/byte cap.</p>
<p>A progress note is presentation, not authority: the model supplies no coordinate, emoji, or cadence, and every line is assembled from operator templates and the run’s own counters. Liveness failures carry only low-cardinality categories and never touch the answer. <a href="/guides/traces/#privacy">Telemetry visibility</a>.</p>
</section>
